      "math_academy_id": "e-14835",
      "problem": "Find the axis of symmetry for the parabola $y=2x^2-12x+3.$",
      "worked_solution": "The equation of the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=ax^2+bx+c$ is given by\n\n$$\nx = -\\dfrac{b}{2a}.\n$$\n\nWe substitute $a=2$ and $b=-12$ into the formula for the axis of symmetry. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{(-12)}{2(2)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{(-12)}{4} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the axis of symmetry is $x=3.$",
